1. Scope
This license applies to the Inventory Pro source code released by Joshua Pond
under this license and to works derived from that code. Components carrying
their own license notices remain subject to their respective licenses.

2. Permitted use
You may run, inspect, copy, modify and distribute the software free of charge.
Internal use in businesses and other commercial organizations is expressly
permitted. Internal modifications do not have to be published.

3. No sale
Without separate written permission from Joshua Pond, you may not sell the
software or derived versions, license them for a fee, distribute them for
payment, or offer them to third parties as a paid hosted service, SaaS product
or managed software instance. This restriction also applies to bundles with
other products or services where payment requires or covers access to
Inventory Pro or a derived version.

Charging for general-purpose computing, storage or network infrastructure and
for independent training, installation or support services is permitted,
provided that no software rights or paid software access are sold. The free
internal use permitted under section 2 is unaffected.

4. Attribution and distribution
Every distribution must retain this license, existing copyright notices,
Joshua Pond's name and a reference to the original project at
https://gitlab.pondsec.com/PondSec/inventorypro. Modified versions must identify
themselves as modified and state the date of modification. Modified
applications must also identify the original author in an accessible About
or License view. You may not falsely imply that the original author endorses
or has approved your version.

Distribution must not restrict these permissions or circumvent the prohibition
on sale. No trademark rights are granted.

5. Warranty and liability
The software is provided without guaranteed properties. To the extent permitted
by law, warranties and liability for damage arising from use, unavailability
or loss of data are excluded. Mandatory legal liability, including liability
for intent, gross negligence, or injury to life, body or health, is unaffected.

6. Earlier versions
This license does not retroactively change rights granted for versions released
under a different license. In particular, versions already published under
AGPL-3.0 remain subject to their original license terms. Because it restricts
sale, this license is not an OSI-approved open-source license.
